    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1310">

                <pb facs="1039" n="923" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg923"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.77/136.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American Ambassador
                        and the American Consuls at Nogales, Ciudad Juárez, Ciudad Porfirio Díaz,
                        Nuevo Laredo, and Matamoros</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Identic telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 14, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In order to prevent any possible misunderstanding of the Department’s May 13, you
                    are informed that the data requested therein was ordered obtained by the
                    President personally, and is desired for the purpose of securing employment in
                    the United States for these idle men.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
